{
  "about": "Battle royale: everyone against everyone, each droid on a side of its own, so nobody has a conversation to have. Each character is a kind of competitor - its name, shown with its code, and the model it is made from - and the droids in a match go round them in turn. Its barks, said out loud as it fights, by when: 'spotted', 'lost', 'heard' and 'gave_up' as it hunts the player; 'engaged' as it goes after anyone; 'downed' when it has shot someone down; 'back' when it comes back after losing a life; and 'ring' when the closing ring catches it outside. Only droids near enough to hear are heard. Its 'chatter' is what it says when the player tries to talk to it: one of them at random, never the same twice running. Every line is checked by data/system_latin/sl_parser.py.",
